Why GPL-3.0-or-later specifically
================================================================================

Version 2.0.0 incorporates algorithms ported from reference security tools whose
licences constrain the choice. The decision is recorded in
docs/adr/0001-relicense-to-gpl-3-0-or-later.md; in brief:

  - katana is GPL-3.0-or-later, which rules out GPLv2.
  - John the Ripper is GPL-2.0-or-later, so it may be used under GPLv3.
  - Upstream CyberChef is Apache-2.0, compatible with GPLv3 but not GPLv2.

GPL-3.0-or-later is the only licence that admits all three simultaneously.

